pivot_wider() for Summary Tables

# Classic use: a summary table with one column per year
gm |&gt;
  filter(year %in% c(1998, 2008), !is.na(life_expectancy)) |&gt;
  group_by(continent, year) |&gt;
  summarize(mean_le = mean(life_expectancy), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  pivot_wider(names_from = year, values_from = mean_le)

# A tibble: 6 × 3
  continent `1998` `2008`
  &lt;chr&gt;      &lt;dbl&gt;  &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Africa      56.3   61.2
2 Americas    72.4   74.4
3 Asia        69.5   72.6
4 Europe      74.9   77.5
5 Oceania     66.4   67.4
6 &lt;NA&gt;        66.0   67.9

A Full Mini-Analysis, End to End

# Which continents improved life expectancy most between 1998 and 2008?
gm |&gt;
  filter(year %in% c(1998, 2008)) |&gt;
  drop_na(life_expectancy) |&gt;
  group_by(continent, year) |&gt;
  summarize(mean_le = mean(life_expectancy), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
  pivot_wider(names_from = year, values_from = mean_le,
              names_prefix = "y") |&gt;
  mutate(gain = y2008 - y1998) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(gain))

# A tibble: 6 × 4
  continent y1998 y2008  gain
  &lt;chr&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Africa     56.3  61.2  4.90
2 Asia       69.5  72.6  3.06
3 Europe     74.9  77.5  2.51
4 Americas   72.4  74.4  2.02
# ℹ 2 more rows


Seven verbs, one readable story: filter → clean → group → summarize → reshape → derive → sort.

arrange(): Ordering Rows

# Lowest child mortality first
gm |&gt;
  filter(year == 2008) |&gt;
  arrange(child_mortality) |&gt;
  select(country, year, child_mortality)  # (select() is next cycle)

# A tibble: 236 × 3
  country           year child_mortality
  &lt;chr&gt;            &lt;dbl&gt;           &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Iceland           2008            2.72
2 Hong Kong, China  2008            2.82
# ℹ 234 more rows

arrange(): Descending Order

# Highest first: wrap in desc()
gm |&gt;
  filter(year == 2008) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(life_expectancy)) |&gt;
  select(country, year, life_expectancy)

# A tibble: 236 × 3
