mutate(): Building on New Columns
New columns can be built from columns you just created:

gm |&gt;
  filter(year == 2008) |&gt;
  select(country, population, GDP_per_capita) |&gt;
  mutate(gdp_millions = GDP_per_capita * population,
         gdp_billions = gdp_millions / 1e3)

# A tibble: 236 × 5
  country     population GDP_per_capita gdp_millions gdp_billions
  &lt;chr&gt;            &lt;dbl&gt;          &lt;dbl&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;
1 Afghanistan      28400          0.492       13973.         14.0
2 Angola           22500          3.96        89100          89.1
# ℹ 234 more rows

mutate() with Logical Columns
A comparison creates a TRUE/FALSE column, ready for later filtering:

gm |&gt;
  filter(year == 2008) |&gt;
  select(country, life_expectancy) |&gt;
  mutate(above_80 = life_expectancy &gt; 80)

# A tibble: 236 × 3
  country     life_expectancy above_80
  &lt;chr&gt;                 &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;lgl&gt;   
1 Afghanistan            59.9 FALSE   
2 Angola                 59.5 FALSE   
